      "legend": "Each cell summarizes all 200 completed adaptation attempts; failed fits remain included and use the prespecified Jeffreys prevalence fallback. Attempts/failed/fallback gives all three counts. Event and loss P05–P95 values are empirical 90% ranges across the 200 draws, not confidence intervals. Losses are evaluated on globally held-out assessment patients and include all assessment stays. These results concern only the completed 50- and 500-label budgets. No-update rows are raw references on the same assessment roster, repeated across the same 200 sampling plans; no calibration fit is attempted (0/0/0). Their event ranges describe the associated adaptation samples. A narrowing model gap may reflect deterioration of a comparator; compare absolute raw and updated losses for both models. The four label budgets are retained in the full source data."
